WEBVTT

00:36.837 --> 00:40.467
Griffin, I need you to run these
shipping reports upstairs to the CEO.

00:40.676 --> 00:43.679
Huh. There's nothing fun
or entertaining about that.

00:43.845 --> 00:46.932
Maybe if I walk down the hall
with a wisecracking rabbi.

00:47.140 --> 00:50.687
- Do you charge a lot for circumcisions?
- No, I just keep the tips.

00:52.189 --> 00:54.441
All right, where's the CEO's office?

00:55.358 --> 00:59.571
Yeah, I've always wanted to see
the inside of the executive bathroom.

01:03.535 --> 01:05.705
- Executive bathroom, sir?
- Uh...

01:05.871 --> 01:08.082
- Yes?
- Right this way.

01:18.052 --> 01:20.805
So, uh, where is this
executive bathroom?

01:21.013 --> 01:22.140
There.

01:39.285 --> 01:42.955
Welcome to
Executive Bathroom Island.

01:49.421 --> 01:51.299
Well, this is peaceful.

01:54.635 --> 01:55.678
Good morning, Lois.

01:55.887 --> 01:58.515
Wow, Peter, since when do you get
so dressed up for work?

01:58.682 --> 02:01.393
Since I got tired of getting nowhere
in this world, Lois.

02:01.560 --> 02:04.439
I've decided to do whatever
it takes to become an executive.

02:04.606 --> 02:07.066
It would certainly be great
if you got a promotion.

02:07.233 --> 02:09.736
You'd earn more money,
get better health insurance.

02:09.903 --> 02:11.864
Lois, I am doing this for the bathroom.

02:12.031 --> 02:15.952
And I'm not giving up on my dream,
like I did with that indoor hot-air balloon.

02:19.664 --> 02:22.667
And away we go.

02:29.342 --> 02:32.721
No, no, no!

02:32.888 --> 02:34.389
I can't feel my legs.

02:34.556 --> 02:35.808
Welcome to the party, pal.

02:35.975 --> 02:38.311
- No, wait. There they are.
Aww...

03:01.630 --> 03:03.966
Boy, it sure is great
to have you back in town.

03:04.132 --> 03:05.592
Yeah, but this place is dead.

03:05.759 --> 03:07.719
I don't know.
That guy seemed to like it.

03:07.928 --> 03:11.349
I like everything, including ginger ale.
Psst.

03:11.516 --> 03:14.270
That's my way
of ordering a ginger ale.

03:15.104 --> 03:17.898
Sorry I can't pay you more,
but business has been bad.

03:18.065 --> 03:19.608
I'm looking to sell the joint.

03:19.817 --> 03:23.280
You can't sell this place.
So few clubs play real music anymore.

03:23.488 --> 03:25.491
Wanna buy it?
I'll give you a good deal.

03:25.700 --> 03:29.494
- You know, that's not a bad idea.
- We could really turn this place around.

03:29.662 --> 03:32.415
It could be bigger than
the Apollo Theater.

03:33.875 --> 03:37.462
All right, now. Next up we got
the comedy stylings of Kim Lee Sung.

03:37.629 --> 03:38.673
Give it up.

03:38.840 --> 03:39.923
How you doing tonight?

03:40.090 --> 03:43.219
Ever notice when two black guy
come in your convenience store...

03:43.386 --> 03:45.430
...one go one way
and one go the other way?

03:45.596 --> 03:48.058
What they doing?
What they stealing? Who with me?

03:50.310 --> 03:51.353
You stay out my store.

03:51.520 --> 03:54.273
All you, stay out my store.
I remember you face.

03:57.277 --> 03:59.030
Peter, I want you to retype those...

03:59.196 --> 04:00.614
Wow, what is this?

04:00.781 --> 04:02.033
Have you been cleaning?

04:02.241 --> 04:04.160
I'm working hard
so you'll promote me.

04:04.326 --> 04:08.165
Based on your record, you'll understand
if I have trouble believing you.

04:08.331 --> 04:11.294
Believe it, Angela.
I hate being just a cog around here.

04:11.461 --> 04:14.505
Almost as much as I hate
homeless people asking me for money.

04:15.046 --> 04:17.842
- Spare some change?
- Sure.

04:18.009 --> 04:20.679
- You didn't put anything in there.
- Yes, I did.

04:20.846 --> 04:22.514
I put hope in there.

04:22.681 --> 04:23.724
Hope.

04:23.892 --> 04:26.019
Don't spend it all in one place, raggie.

04:29.481 --> 04:31.274
Griffin, what the hell is this?

04:31.441 --> 04:34.111
It's a robot that I built
to save this company money.

04:34.278 --> 04:37.199
Now, before you say anything,
one, it has no human emotions.

04:37.365 --> 04:40.827
And two, its prime directive
is never to harm people.

04:40.994 --> 04:42.871
Oh. Oh, God. It's harming people.

04:43.038 --> 04:44.957
<i>Angry. Angry.</i>

04:45.124 --> 04:48.294
Oh, God.
It's got human emotions too.

04:48.461 --> 04:52.048
Aah! It's using tools.
It's learning, Angela. It's learning.

04:52.215 --> 04:53.550
Run!

04:56.386 --> 04:57.680
What do you want, Griffin?

04:57.889 --> 04:58.932
Look out your window.

04:59.098 --> 05:02.268
See that Anheuser-Busch billboard
next to the children's hospital?

05:02.435 --> 05:04.020
Well, watch this.

05:05.856 --> 05:07.608
Oh, God.

05:07.775 --> 05:09.861
Oh, my God. This is horrible.

05:10.028 --> 05:12.906
Oh, God. Oh, that's terrible.

05:13.073 --> 05:15.367
Oh, good Lord, save them.
Bless their lit...

05:15.534 --> 05:17.327
Oh, okay, okay, yeah.

05:17.494 --> 05:20.039
Here we go.
All right, everything worked out.

05:22.751 --> 05:24.920
<i>We now return to Matt Damon...</i>

05:25.087 --> 05:27.673
<i>...and Leonardo DiCaprio
in The Detarded.</i>

05:27.881 --> 05:29.174
<i>You're under arrest.</i>

05:29.341 --> 05:31.386
<i>No, you're under arrest.</i>

05:37.309 --> 05:38.351
Stewie, guess what.

05:38.518 --> 05:41.939
Frank and I just closed a deal
to buy the Quahog Cabana Club.

05:42.106 --> 05:44.943
Oh, wow, Brian, what else are you
doing that's terrible and stupid?

05:45.110 --> 05:48.573
Just wait. In a few weeks, that club
will be the hottest spot in Quahog.

05:48.781 --> 05:50.198
Huh. You're deluding yourself.

05:50.365 --> 05:53.911
You're gonna fail faster than
John Madden's wedding-video business.

05:56.123 --> 05:58.125
<i>Boom, here's your groom over here.</i>

05:58.292 --> 06:00.044
<i>Boom, you got your bride right here.</i>

06:00.211 --> 06:02.671
<i>A lot of people say
that Stacy's no good...</i>

06:02.838 --> 06:05.883
<i>...and that she slept with this guy,
and done that guy...</i>

06:06.050 --> 06:08.053
<i>...and even did some handwork
on this guy.</i>

06:08.220 --> 06:11.557
<i>I'll tell you, that is gonna work
in her favor late in the game.</i>

06:11.724 --> 06:14.810
<i>You know who had a heck of a wedding?
Brett Favre.</i>

06:18.606 --> 06:20.443
Griffin, I've got good news.

06:20.651 --> 06:22.695
A management position
has become available.

06:22.862 --> 06:25.531
And I've seen that you've been
working very hard lately.

06:25.698 --> 06:27.742
I am recommending you
for a promotion.

06:27.908 --> 06:30.620
- I get to use the executive bathroom?
- Of course.

06:30.787 --> 06:34.334
Holy crap. You know, last week
I ate a fortune cookie that said:

06:34.500 --> 06:37.295
"Obvious lesbian
will bring great news. "

06:37.462 --> 06:40.923
It also said a grand piano
will fall on me.

06:42.843 --> 06:44.386
Well, good day to you.

06:44.553 --> 06:46.723
And I will, um...

06:46.890 --> 06:49.559
Uh, yeah. I mean, we're done.

06:49.726 --> 06:53.396
Just, uh, squeeze by you here.

06:56.650 --> 06:59.863
Is this where I get the poop pass
to use the executive bathroom?

07:00.071 --> 07:01.572
Sit down. We need to talk.

07:01.739 --> 07:04.242
Well, make it fast,
because I'm starting to crown.

07:04.451 --> 07:07.622
Mr. Griffin, all our executives
require a high school education.

07:07.789 --> 07:10.751
And your file says
that you never passed the third grade.

07:10.918 --> 07:13.878
If you want this,
you'll have to go back and finish.

07:14.087 --> 07:17.007
Well, that sounds hilarious,
but it also might take a while.

07:17.174 --> 07:18.885
I'm afraid that's your only option.

07:19.052 --> 07:22.347
Well, I mean, if that's what I gotta do,
then I guess I...

07:25.183 --> 07:28.687
Next time you get a fortune cookie,
don't open it.

07:39.992 --> 07:41.869
Bye, you guys. Have fun at school.

07:42.036 --> 07:43.579
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

07:43.789 --> 07:45.165
Oh, Peter, stop pouting.

07:45.332 --> 07:48.585
All you gotta do is finish third grade
and you'll get that promotion.

07:48.752 --> 07:50.963
Oh... This is gonna be a bigger pain...

07:51.129 --> 07:53.967
...than getting into a last-clap contest
with Cleveland.

07:54.175 --> 07:58.222
Ladies and gentlemen,
the Quahog Men's Chorus.

08:05.689 --> 08:06.773
Hey, hey, hey.

08:06.940 --> 08:09.110
Clap one more time,
you're not coming to my birthday.

08:10.528 --> 08:11.945
- Who did that?
Giggity.

08:15.116 --> 08:16.534
Good morning, class.

08:16.742 --> 08:18.745
Starting today,
we have a new student.

08:18.912 --> 08:21.624
Peter, would you like to
introduce yourself?

08:21.833 --> 08:23.584
Hi, my name's Peter Griffin. Um...

08:23.750 --> 08:27.171
I was actually in third grade
a long time ago, but I never finished.

08:27.338 --> 08:29.717
Back then we had a teacher
named Mrs. Wilson.

08:29.883 --> 08:32.511
Ha-ha. Except we had
this funny little nickname for her.

08:32.678 --> 08:35.848
We called her "Mrs. Kill-Son"
because she had an abortion.

08:36.015 --> 08:39.185
I know it's kind of silly,
but we were just a bunch of kids.

08:39.352 --> 08:41.313
I'm sorry. Go ahead, Mrs., uh...?

08:41.521 --> 08:43.899
Wilson. Thank you, Peter.

08:44.108 --> 08:46.611
Why don't you sit over there
next to Omar?

08:47.862 --> 08:49.739
Omar is our top student.

08:49.905 --> 08:54.286
And we're hoping he'll lead us to victory
next week in the district spelling bee.

08:54.495 --> 08:57.749
What are you doing? You're old.
Are you stupid or something?

08:57.914 --> 08:59.584
Oh, picking on the new kid, huh?

08:59.751 --> 09:02.420
Well, at least my parents
didn't name me "Gaymar. "

09:04.048 --> 09:07.344
Wow. I never knew you could make fun
of someone for being homosexual.

09:07.510 --> 09:09.762
And by laughing at
other people's sexuality...

09:09.928 --> 09:12.182
...somehow I feel better
about my own.

09:19.231 --> 09:20.776
Brian, where are all the people?

09:20.942 --> 09:22.943
They'll be here.
We gotta give them time.

09:23.152 --> 09:25.906
And wouldn't you know it?
There's our first customer.

09:26.073 --> 09:28.826
I'll entertain him
while we wait for more to arrive.

09:28.993 --> 09:31.162
So thanks for coming.
How you doing tonight?

09:31.371 --> 09:33.165
Good.

09:33.373 --> 09:34.832
Glad to hear it. Any requests?

09:35.041 --> 09:37.378
Play "On the Dark Side"...

09:37.544 --> 09:41.091
...by John Cafferty
and the Beaver Brown Band.

09:41.257 --> 09:42.550
Give it up, Brian.

09:42.717 --> 09:45.512
No one wants to go to
a stupid big-band club anymore.

09:45.678 --> 09:49.517
I could help make some changes around
here that would bring in customers.

09:49.683 --> 09:52.436
You know, we should give Stewie
a shot. It can't hurt.

09:52.603 --> 09:54.689
Well, what did you have in mind?

09:54.898 --> 09:56.983
Just trust me.
I know exactly what to do.

09:57.150 --> 09:58.485
You've gotta be aggressive.

09:58.693 --> 10:02.907
More aggressive than Michael Jackson's
treatment of his own groin onstage.

10:13.001 --> 10:15.130
Hee-hee.

10:21.469 --> 10:22.805
Thank you.

10:26.184 --> 10:29.146
All right, Susie. What have you
brought in for show-and-tell?

10:29.354 --> 10:32.482
This is my Malibu Barbie doll
that I got for Christmas this year.

10:32.649 --> 10:36.612
She comes with a hairbrush,
a pocketbook and two different dresses.

10:36.779 --> 10:40.284
Oh, my God. Who the hell cares?

10:40.492 --> 10:43.538
Peter, I would like to remind you
that you are in a classroom.

10:43.746 --> 10:45.164
Not for long.

10:47.876 --> 10:48.918
Can I help you, sir?

10:49.127 --> 10:50.545
Hi. My name's Glenn Griffin.

10:50.712 --> 10:54.258
Uh, I'm here to pick up my son Peter
for a ball ga... Uh, doctor's appointment.

10:54.425 --> 10:56.886
- Peter is your son?
- That is affirmative.

10:57.052 --> 10:59.723
Because you look
a lot more like that child over there.

11:00.473 --> 11:02.684
- Daddy?
- Oh, God.

11:05.396 --> 11:07.982
- Daddy?
- Oh, God.

11:10.735 --> 11:12.362
<i>- Papб?
- Oh, God.</i>

11:14.656 --> 11:17.577
- Hey, there are no kids in here, right?
- No. Just me.

11:17.785 --> 11:19.203
Oh, thank God.

11:19.369 --> 11:21.122
You wanna have unprotected sex?

11:21.289 --> 11:22.457
Hmm...

11:37.391 --> 11:39.477
What the hell
did Stewie do to this place?

11:39.644 --> 11:42.147
Hey, get a load of
Maynard G. Krebs over here.

11:42.314 --> 11:44.190
He's rubbing the records
with his hand.

11:44.357 --> 11:46.985
Hey, hey.
You're gonna ruin that, you know.

11:47.194 --> 11:49.530
I'm sorry, I shouldn't have
called you a name.

11:49.697 --> 11:52.408
Here, take some of these
for your 45s.

11:52.575 --> 11:55.536
You can't play your 45s
without these little yellow things.

11:55.703 --> 11:57.873
What'll they make you buy next?

11:58.082 --> 12:00.250
Hey, hey. There they are.

12:00.417 --> 12:03.338
Stewie, what is all this?
What did you do to the Cabana Club?

12:03.546 --> 12:06.133
Oh, we don't call it
the Cabana Club anymore, Frank.

12:06.300 --> 12:08.718
It's now called pLace. Little P, big L.

12:08.927 --> 12:12.348
Congratulations. You two now own
the hottest spot in town.

12:12.556 --> 12:16.019
Wow, that's a lot of people.
I hope we have enough rye.

12:16.228 --> 12:17.562
How'd you pay for all this?

12:17.729 --> 12:20.482
I got a job as a field reporter
for Channel 5 News.

12:20.691 --> 12:22.526
<i>All the juice is collected underneath?</i>

12:22.694 --> 12:26.531
<i>Yes. And whoever collects the most
is gonna win a free weekend here...</i>

12:26.698 --> 12:28.992
<i>...with international foods
and wine tasting.</i>

12:29.159 --> 12:32.204
<i>Stop. Oho... Oof!</i>

12:32.371 --> 12:34.289
<i>Oh!</i>

12:34.456 --> 12:36.918
<i>Ow, ow, ow!</i>

12:39.922 --> 12:43.007
<i>Oh, I can't breathe. I can't breathe.
Ow, ow, ow.</i>

12:44.802 --> 12:47.179
Ooh. Oh, gosh. I hope he's all right.

12:47.346 --> 12:49.850
We'll have to send someone
to make sure that he is.

12:54.062 --> 12:56.691
- Hey, Omar, want a Hertz doughnut?
- Um...

12:56.858 --> 12:58.317
Okay.

12:58.526 --> 13:01.530
Hurts, don't it? Ha-ha-ha. Dumb-ass.

13:01.738 --> 13:04.951
Wow, he effectively silenced Omar
by hitting him in the face.

13:05.118 --> 13:09.038
My dad hits me.
But I bet if I hit others, the pain stops.

13:09.205 --> 13:11.875
Someday, I'll use
what I've learned here on my wife.

13:12.083 --> 13:14.670
Peter, is this your homework?

13:14.837 --> 13:17.214
Hold on.
Let me take out my reading glasses.

13:19.258 --> 13:21.011
Ha-ha-ha. Yeah, that's mine.

13:21.219 --> 13:22.679
I could flunk you for this.

13:22.846 --> 13:25.349
But "buttlickers"
is a three-syllable word.

13:25.516 --> 13:27.643
Not even Omar can spell those.

13:27.810 --> 13:31.314
So you're joining him
at next week's district spelling bee.

13:31.480 --> 13:33.358
If you lead our school to victory...

13:33.525 --> 13:35.319
...I'll let you pass third grade.

13:35.485 --> 13:37.404
But if you lose, you fail.

13:37.614 --> 13:39.240
I accept that challenge.

13:39.407 --> 13:42.285
Late '70s Bruce Jenner,
take me home.

13:42.452 --> 13:44.537
Hop on, Peter.

13:59.222 --> 14:02.141
Brian, how does it feel to own
the coolest club in Quahog?

14:02.308 --> 14:04.477
You think this is cool?
Look at these people.

14:04.644 --> 14:07.689
I'd rather go bankrupt
than cater to jerks like this.

14:07.856 --> 14:10.025
Whoa, Brian. Slow down, man.

14:10.192 --> 14:14.405
We're making money now.
And besides, this place ain't all bad.

14:14.572 --> 14:16.241
Hey, you girls thirsty?

14:16.407 --> 14:18.660
Could I interest you
in a couple of Rob Roys?

14:18.826 --> 14:22.831
- What's a Rob Roy?
- Only the drink of Mr. Peter Lawford.

14:22.998 --> 14:24.167
Who's Peter Lawford?

14:24.334 --> 14:26.419
What am I hitting on,
Lou Costello here?

14:26.586 --> 14:28.171
Who's Lou Costello?

14:28.338 --> 14:32.051
Uh, sorry, my friend's a little new
to the club scene.

14:32.259 --> 14:34.387
Jeez, what the hell's
with these broads?

14:34.553 --> 14:37.349
Look at you two.
Tuxes in a nightclub?

14:37.557 --> 14:40.727
<i>You're more out of place
than Prince was on The Price Is Right.</i>

14:40.936 --> 14:43.397
And what's your bid
on the dining-room set, Prince?

14:43.605 --> 14:45.066
Three-fifty.
- I'm sorry?

14:45.274 --> 14:47.694
- Three-fif...
- Can you speak up, please?

14:47.902 --> 14:48.988
Three-fifty.

14:49.196 --> 14:54.952
All right. And the actual retail price
of the dining-room set is $350.

14:55.160 --> 14:56.997
Yay.

15:01.419 --> 15:04.379
- Peter, wake up.
- Huh? Wha...? Oh. Oh.

15:04.546 --> 15:06.716
Oh, Lois.
I just had the weirdest dream.

15:06.882 --> 15:09.010
Lewis Black told jokes
that were so funny...

15:09.177 --> 15:11.471
...he had to shout them
so everyone could hear.

15:11.638 --> 15:14.600
Peter, you gotta stay awake.
The spelling bee's tomorrow.

15:14.809 --> 15:16.143
But, Lois, I'm scared.

15:16.309 --> 15:18.813
There's no way I can compete
against those kids.

15:18.980 --> 15:21.190
It's like trying
to beat Schpupel champion...

15:21.357 --> 15:23.819
...Fjurg van der Ploeg
at a game of Schpupel.

15:33.246 --> 15:34.290
Schpupel.

15:36.751 --> 15:40.296
Don't be sad, Peter.
That's why they call it Schpupel.

15:42.966 --> 15:44.259
God, we look like idiots.

15:44.426 --> 15:47.472
Hey, hey. That's more like it.
Where'd you get the threads?

15:47.638 --> 15:48.765
We went to Barneys.

15:48.931 --> 15:51.934
I heard that's where all the people shop
for skinny-leg jeans.

15:52.518 --> 15:55.856
Whoa, these are the tightest,
penis-compressingest...

15:56.023 --> 15:59.569
...sperm-killingest, testicle-grippingest
jeans I ever tried on.

15:59.778 --> 16:02.654
Brian, Frank,
meet Dakota and New Bedford.

16:02.821 --> 16:04.574
Hey, how's it hanging, Dakota?

16:04.741 --> 16:05.950
What's up, New Bedford?

16:06.117 --> 16:08.329
You look like rappers,
but you're not black.

16:08.496 --> 16:10.372
So that's
the perfect amount of danger.

16:10.539 --> 16:12.417
Listen, you guys
get to know each other.

16:12.584 --> 16:14.960
Looks like my doorman
let another gazelle in here.

16:16.004 --> 16:17.839
Sorry,
but we've been over this before.

16:18.006 --> 16:21.177
- We don't serve your kind here.
- You're gonna hear from my lawyer.

16:21.344 --> 16:24.348
Yeah? I would welcome that.
I would welcome the opportunity...

16:24.515 --> 16:28.227
...to hear from a lawyer that represents
a gazelle. What's his name?

16:28.393 --> 16:30.729
Yeah, I don't have a lawyer.

16:33.024 --> 16:34.859
I'll tell you about Dean Martin.

16:35.026 --> 16:37.946
He was the only guy on the golf course
who had a 5-iron...

16:38.112 --> 16:39.656
...with a cork on the end of it.

16:41.659 --> 16:45.205
So, uh, who wants to come back to the
hotel and take a whack at my genitals?

16:45.372 --> 16:46.581
- Cool.
- Awesome.

16:46.748 --> 16:48.416
All right, we got a ball game.

16:48.583 --> 16:51.545
Hang on, girls.
I'll get you a couple of appletinis.

16:51.711 --> 16:54.465
This is going great, Frank.
This club and these clothes.

16:54.632 --> 16:56.634
My God,
there's nothing that can stop us.

16:56.842 --> 16:58.720
Hey, party people!

16:58.887 --> 17:00.597
I'm ready to get eighty-sixed.

17:02.057 --> 17:03.600
- Andy Dick?
- Oh, no.

17:03.767 --> 17:05.937
Come on. Let's get out of here.

17:09.565 --> 17:11.235
What the hell just happened?

17:11.402 --> 17:13.027
Andy Dick happened.

17:13.194 --> 17:15.072
As soon as that guy
shows up anyplace...

17:15.239 --> 17:17.700
...it gets a worse rap
than John Wilkes Booth.

